t accepted. Do calculations and row operations by hand. Problem 16 must use a different matrix from the textbook answer. Show required explanations and proofs." "**MTH 341 — Written Homework 2**\n\nDue: 2026-10-14\nDue time: 11:59 p.m. PDT\nDeadline verified: 2026-10-12\nDeadline source: [Canvas assignment](https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2064363/assignments/10695094)\nDate imported: 2026-10-12\nSource: [341-WHW-2.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FWHW-2%2F341-WHW-2.pdf)\nTextbook: [A First Course in Linear Algebra, Version 2017 Revision A](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F341%2FKuttler-LinearAlgebra-AFirstCourse-2017A.pdf), Lyryx Learning, based on K. Kuttler. Exercise wording is from this CC BY textbook.\n\nThe downloaded assignment sheet bears an old Spring 2022/2023 heading and an April 13 deadline; these are historical source details. The current deadline above is verified in Fall 2026 Canvas.\n\nStudy answers and worked explanations are authored additions; source-provided answers are identified where used.\n\n## Instructions\n\nUse separate 8.5×11-inch or A4 paper, and use the assignment sheet as the cover with your name and student ID. Submit on Canvas; the sheet states that late work is not accepted. Do calculations and row operations by hand. Problem 16 must use a different matrix from the textbook answer. Show required explanations and proofs."] [:db/cas 17592186484490 :tutorial/content "**MTH 256 — Written Homework 2**\n\nDue: 2026-10-16\nDue time: 11:59 p.m. PDT\nDeadline verified: 2026-10-12\nDeadline source: [Canvas assignment](https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2064169/assignments/10722761)\nDate imported: 2026-10-12\nSource: [256-WHW2.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FWHW-2%2F256-WHW2.pdf)\n\nStudy answers and worked explanations are authored additions; source-provided answers are identified where used.\n\n## Instructions\n\nShow your work and retain the source exercise numbers. The authored study explanations use the standard local criteria: continuity of $f$ on a neighborhood guarantees existence, and continuity of both $f$ and $f_y$ on a neighborhood guarantees uniqueness. The partial-derivative prerequisite is a verified MVC lesson outside the usual MTH 256 route. In Problems 1–2, determine where the cited theorem guarantees existence or uniqueness; do not equate failure of its hypotheses with failure of a solution. For Problems 3–4 use the supplied homogeneous-equation substitution." "**MTH 256 — Written Homework 2**\n\nDue: 2026-10-16\nDue time: 11:59 p.m. PDT\nDeadline verified: 2026-10-12\nDeadline source: [Canvas assignment](https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2064169/assignments/10722761)\nDate imported: 2026-10-12\nSource: [256-WHW-2.pdf](/api/source?path=%2Fhome%2Fjake%2FDeveloper%2Fstudy%2Fvault%2FF26%2Fsource%2F256%2FWHW-2%2F256-WHW-2.pdf)\n\nStudy answers and worked explanations are authored additions; source-provided answers are identified where used.\n\n## Instructions\n\nShow your work and retain the source exercise numbers. The authored study explanations use the standard local criteria: continuity of $f$ on a neighborhood guarantees existence, and continuity of both $f$ and $f_y$ on a neighborhood guarantees uniqueness. The partial-derivative prerequisite is a verified MVC lesson outside the usual MTH 256 route. In Problems 1–2, determine where the cited theorem guarantees existence or uniqueness; do not equate failure of its hypotheses with failure of a solution. For Problems 3–4 use the supplied homogeneous-equation substitution."] [:db/cas 17592186484525 :tutorial/content "**MTH 256 — Recitation Activity 3**\n\nDue: 2026-10-14\nDue time: 11:59 p.m. PDT\nDeadline verified: 2026-10-12\nDeadline source: [Canvas assignment](https://canvas.oregonstate.edu/courses/2064169/assignments/10722757)\nDate imported: 2026-10-12\nSource: [25